## Key findings (read before diagnosing any page)
- **Nov 5 surge:** site impressions rose about 2.2x (134k to 302k a day) while clicks stayed flat (about 550 to 720 a day). CTR fell from about 0.44% to 0.21%. It is a ranking jump on broad head terms, not a title problem, and it began before any edit in this project.
- **Where clicks are:** pages at position 2.5 or better hold 44% of impressions at 0.07% CTR. Pages at 5.5 to 10.5 get about 0.43%. Title and meta work pays in the blue-link zone (position 3.5 or lower).
- **Earlier impression waves reverted** within about 10 days (Sep 16 to 24, Oct 12 to 15). Judge by clicks per day, never CTR, and expect a possible reversal. Bump pages are the most exposed to a reversal, so update them first.
- **Clicks fell on Nov 12** (362 against 597 on Nov 11), during the Google core update that began Nov 10. The Nov 13 daily row is partial. Re-check in about 7 days before reading any result.
- **Nail-art pair decision:** `/topics/nail-art-guides` and `/blog/mirelle-inspo-nail-art-ideas` overlap on "nail art ideas" but earn no split clicks and do not swap positions. **No 301.** Pending: one cross-link each way and an inlinks anchor audit.
- **Deadlines:** Thanksgiving Nov 26, Christmas Dec 25, New Year's Eve Dec 31. Title and meta changes show in 1 to 3 weeks, content in 2 to 6.

